    "text": "The second route runs through Russia's own neighbors. Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan and Armenia share a customs union with Russia, so goods can cross their borders with few checks. One analysis found that Kazakhstan sold about eleven thousand euros worth of semiconductor parts to Russia in twenty twenty one. The next year, it was three point three million. Turkey and the United Arab Emirates became hubs too, for banking, for reshipping, and for traders who knew how to make paperwork look clean.",
